{#
_partials/_segmented.html.twig
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The segmented control Settings uses for a choice among a few options: On/Off,
or three or four named ones. A row of radios drawn as one rounded strip,
with the checked one filled in the accent colour.

One macro instead of a copy in every settings card. There were about thirty, each
with its own `segGroup` and `segText` strings, and they had already drifted:
`px-2` here and `px-3` there, `w-28` on some, `max-w-md` on others, a `label`
with `cursor-pointer` on half of them. A fix to the focus ring had to be made
thirty times or not at all.

How the choice is saved is the caller's, passed in as attributes, because
there are three ways and the control should not know which:
  - posted on its own by settings--toggle, with `data-key` on each radio
    (AI, insights, labels);
  - submitting the form it sits in through ui--auto-submit (disposal, pinning);
  - part of a form saved with a button.

    {% import '_partials/_segmented.html.twig' as seg %}
    {{ seg.control('labels-by_account', [
        { value: '1', label: 'settings.labels.seg.on'|trans },
        { value: '0', label: 'settings.labels.seg.off'|trans },
    ], user.labelsByAccount ? '1' : '0', {
        label:  'Labels by account',
        width:  'w-28',
        action: 'change->settings--toggle#toggle',
        data:   { key: 'by_account' },
    }) }}

Arguments:
  name     the radios' name, shared by the group and posted as the field name
  options  list of { value, label, attrs? }: `label` already translated,
           `attrs` extra data-* for that one radio as a map
  current  the value that is checked. Compared as strings: Twig hands over
           array keys '1' and '0' as integers, and a switch must not end up
           with nothing checked because 1 is not '1'
  opts     label       the group's accessible name (or labelledby: an id)
           width       width class for the strip; defaults to shrink-0 with
                       equal columns, which sizes to the longest option
           action      data-action on every radio
           data        data-* on every radio, as a map
           form        a form id, for a radio outside its form
#}
{% macro control(name, options, current, opts = {}) %}
    {%- set _label      = opts.label ?? null -%}
    {%- set _labelledby = opts.labelledby ?? null -%}
    <div class="grid grid-flow-col auto-cols-fr {{ opts.width ?? 'shrink-0' }} rounded-pane border border-line overflow-hidden"
         role="radiogroup"
         {% if _labelledby %}aria-labelledby="{{ _labelledby }}"{% elseif _label %}aria-label="{{ _label }}"{% endif %}
         data-segmented="{{ name }}">
        {% for option in options %}
            <label class="cursor-pointer">
                <input type="radio" name="{{ name }}" class="peer sr-only"
                       value="{{ option.value }}"
                       {% if opts.action ?? null %}data-action="{{ opts.action }}"{% endif %}
                       {% if opts.form ?? null %}form="{{ opts.form }}"{% endif %}
                       {% for key, value in opts.data ?? {} %}data-{{ key }}="{{ value }}" {% endfor %}
                       {% for key, value in option.attrs ?? {} %}data-{{ key }}="{{ value }}" {% endfor %}
                       aria-label="{{ _label ? _label ~ ' — ' : '' }}{{ option.label }}"
                       {{ (current ~ '') == (option.value ~ '') ? 'checked' : '' }}>
                <span class="flex h-full items-center justify-center px-2 py-1.5 text-center text-[11px] leading-tight text-ink-muted
                             peer-checked:bg-accent peer-checked:text-accent-ink
                             peer-focus-visible:ring-2 peer-focus-visible:ring-inset peer-focus-visible:ring-accent
                             transition-colors">{{ option.label }}</span>
            </label>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
{% endmacro %}
